    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "in a couple days. They said that. I don't know if that's really true. But the technology of it and this constant push for speed and data and access to information and pulling things together is what's so vital. So I love our national laboratories. Illinois has a lot of challenges, but I'm so proud of a couple things. One is the fact that we have two fabulous national laboratories, Fermilab and Argonne, which are absolutely on the forefront of science, but also the work that they do with our universities, with University of Chicago, with Northwestern, University of Illinois, Northern Illinois University. There is some great, great cooperation and opportunity for people to be engaged in gaining their education, but also working on literally cutting edge world leading science projects. It's one of my favorite things when I go to Fermilab and Cole and I love going there. We used to live just a little ways away, so Cole and his brother would ride their bikes and I would Yell, slow down, wait for me, trying to keep up with them. But it's a beautiful place. But also one of the things that I love is walking into their different research projects that they've got. And they've got a listing of all the universities that are tied in. And sometimes it's dozens of different universities. that have a direct, direct connection of work that's happening in our national laboratory. So it honestly is this ecosystem of science and research that works. There's things that the federal government needs to do. There's a lot of things private sector can do and we're certainly seeing that in space with great advancement there. Love a lot of the private sector investment in space, but I still think we need a vibrant NASA. We need vibrant laboratories to be working well. We need to do everything that we can to encourage smart, young people to say these are great fields to go into. And I love it too that you can use that technology and programming along with a vital role in our markets and free enterprise. To me it's a great intersection and I just want to continue to champion that.",
